character length\n- Uses fixed decimal places for all numbers\n- Pads nulls to match numeric width\n\n### 4. `/workspace/FracturedJson/Formatter.cs`\nUpdated two locations where `TableTemplate` is instantiated:\n- Line 283: Compact array formatting\n- Line 356: Table formatting\n\nChanged from:\n```csharp\nvar template = new TableTemplate(_pads, !Options.DontJustifyNumbers);\n```\n\nTo:\n```csharp\nvar shouldJustifyNumbers = !Options.DontJustifyNumbers && Options.NumberListAlignment != NumberListAlignment.Left;\nvar template = new TableTemplate(_pads, shouldJustifyNumbers, Options.NumberListAlignment);\n```\n\nUpdated `InlineTableRowSegment()` to handle null values with alignment:\n```csharp\nelse if (template.IsFormattableNumber && item.Type == JsonItemType.Null)\n{\n    _buffer.Add(template.FormatNumber(item.Value, isNull: true));\n}\n```\n\n### 5. `/workspace/Tests/NumberFormattingTests.cs`\nAdded 13 comprehensive test cases:\n- `NumberListAlignmentLeft` - Basic left alignment\n- `NumberListAlignmentLeftWithNull` - Left alignment with null values\n- `NumberListAlignmentRight` - Basic right alignment (default behavior)\n- `NumberListAlignmentRightWithNull` - Right alignment with null values\n- `NumberListAlignmentDecimal` - Decimal point alignment\n- `NumberListAlignmentDecimalWithNull` - Decimal alignment with nulls\n- `NumberListAlignmentDecimalTable` - Decimal alignment in table format\n- `NumberListAlignmentNormalize` - Normalize mode\n- `NumberListAlignmentNormalizeWithNull` - Normalize with nulls\n- `NumberListAlignmentNormalizeRowsHaveEqualLength` - Verifies equal row lengths\n- `NumberListAlignmentDecimalLargeNumbers` - Tests with large numbers\n- `NumberListAlignmentDecimalNegativeNumbers` - Tests with negative values\n- `NumberListAlignmentNestedArrays` - Tests nested array alignment\n\n### 6. `/workspace/Tests/UniversalJsonTests.cs`\nUpdated all option combinations in `GenerateOptions()` to use:\n```csharp\nNumberListAlignment = NumberListAlignment.Decimal\n```\nThis ensures all universal tests validate decimal-point alignment behavior.\n\n## Behavior Details\n\n### Left Mode\n- Numbers formatted with consistent decimal places\n- Left-justified within column\n- Right-padded with spaces\n- Null treated as literal \"null\", right-padded\n\n### Right Mode (Default)\n- Numbers formatted with consistent decimal places\n- Right-justified within column\n- Left-padded with spaces\n- Null treated as literal \"null\", left-padded\n- Maintains backward compatibility\n\n### Decimal Mode\n- Decimal points aligned vertically across rows\n- Computed based on maximum digits before/after decimal\n- Spaces inserted before/after as needed\n- Null left-padded to align with decimal position\n\n### Normalize Mode\n- All numbers have identical width\n- Fixed decimal places for all values\n- Guarantees rows have equal character length\n- Useful for fixed-width output requirements\n\n## Nesting Support\nThe alignment mode is applied consistently at all nesting depths because:\n1. The `NumberListAlignment` option is passed from `Formatter` to `TableTemplate`\n2. `TableTemplate` passes the alignment mode to all child templates\n3. Alignment is computed per-column at each level independently\n\n## Compatibility\n- Existing `DontJustifyNumbers` option still works\n- When `DontJustifyNumbers = true`, alignment is disabled\n- When `NumberListAlignment = Left`, numbers are not reformatted (treated as strings)\n- Default `NumberListAlignment = Right` maintains existing behavior\n- All other options (line length, EOL style, whitespace omission) are respected\n\n## Testing\nThe implementation includes comprehensive tests covering:\n- All four alignment modes\n- Null value handling\n- Large numbers\n- Negative numbers\n- Scientific notation (invalidates alignment as expected)\n- Nested arrays\n- Table formatting\n- Row length equality for Normalize mode\nEOF\ncat /tmp/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md",
